fix: review round 10 -- declare-before-call bug, retention effective-freed accounting, launcher identity gate, lsblk PKNAME, cross-component config consistency

Critical bug fixes (review round 10):
1. test-recovery.sh: cached_of() was declared AFTER its first call (line 132 vs
   187) -- under `set -e` this aborts with code 127 before any verdict. Moved
   the definition above first use; added tests/test_script_order.py as a
   static guard that catches declare-after-call patterns in every bash script
   (verified the guard actually fires on a synthetic buggy script).
2. retention.py: select_victims() and eviction_report() counted naive
   bytes_on_disk as freed, contradicting effective_freed_bytes semantics
   (shared entries free 0 bytes until their last reference goes). Now both use
   effective freed bytes (0 for shared_refs > 1), with the nominal sum kept
   separately in the report for transparency. Module docstring now states the
   LIMITATION honestly: shared_refs is a logical hint, not a verified
   cross-namespace physical-object refcount aligned with LMCache -- "freed"
   numbers are lower bounds, not guarantees.
3. run-vllm-with-persist.sh: verify-engine-identity.sh gate is now a
   mandatory step BEFORE --kv-transfer-config is attached to vLLM (previously
   only called in test-recovery.sh). MISMATCH (exit 4) or INCONCLUSIVE (exit 5)
   refuse to launch with persistent cache; KVP_PERSIST_ENABLED=0 is the
   documented bypass. This is the "mandatory barrier" the review asked for.
4. test-recovery.sh disk_read_bytes(): replaced the regex-split device
   normalization (broken on /dev/nvme0n1p1 -> "nvme0n") with lsblk PKNAME
   resolution, falling back to findmnt -- robust for VM-style vda/sda names.
5. start-cache.sh: L2 adapter template path now uses the exported
   KVP_MODEL_CONFIG (was hardcoded to mimo-v2.6-pro), matching the universal
   model-config selector added earlier.
6. docs/final-report.md (and RU/ZH): stale commit hash replaced with a
   `git rev-parse HEAD` self-reference (no more fixed-hash drift); test counts
   synced to 59 (the real pytest-collected count).
7. README (all locales): removed lingering "4-GPU host" phrasing -- now says
   "a target GPU host" per the universal-configuration directive.

New tests (all green, 59 collected):
- tests/test_script_order.py: shell functions must be declared before use.
- tests/test_config_consistency.py: scripts/env.sh (shell seeder),
  implementation/kvpersist/config.py (Python loader) and the launcher/verify
  path must agree on .local overlay, env-wins precedence and multi-model
  ambiguity refusal -- drives all three on a synthetic layout.